Support JP2 images as conversion sources
Convertster should accept JP2 files as source images while keeping JP2 unsupported as an output format. Existing JPG and PNG conversion settings should remain unchanged.

- **Decoding:** Use Magick.NET for `.jp2` inputs, then pass the decoded image to ImageSharp for output encoding.
  ```csharp
  using var jp2Image = new MagickImage(filename);
  using var pngStream = new MemoryStream(jp2Image.ToByteArray(MagickFormat.Png));
  return await Image.LoadAsync(pngStream, token);
  ```
